/*  The file that makes `examples/garden/` a project — lesson 11 of `docs/TUTORIAL.md`.

    Its LOCATION does the first job: a folder with a `blueprint.cufe` in it is a project, so
    `garden.cufe` sees `bed` from `beds.cufe` with nothing pulled. Its CONTENTS do the second:
    `cufet build`, run in this folder, builds what the steps describe.

    `needs` came from `cufet pulls garden.cufe`, which reports the files the program really loads.
    Paths are relative to this folder.
*/

Pull a book on blueprints.
    Bind series of step to blueprint:
        Return a series of step with (
            a record with (
                the name "garden",
                the needs a series of text with ("garden.cufe", "beds.cufe"),
                the makes a series of text with ("garden.exe"),
                the runs a series of text with ("cufet", "build", "garden.cufe"))).
    Done.
Done.
